            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. A DC fan sets its speed electronically and must be controlled with its own remote or the manufacturer's compatible wall control. Feed it from a plain on and off switch left in the on position. A dimmer or conventional fan speed control can cause erratic operation and can damage the fan's controller, which is costly to replace."
          }
